      "updated": 1792485689470,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The foundational paper for modern RLHF. It established how to train a separate neural network\nreward model from human pairwise comparisons of trajectory segments (       ), which is then used\nto optimize the policy. The reward model optimizes the Bradley-Terry preference probability:",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The foundational paper for modern RLHF. It established how to train a separate neural network reward model from human pairwise comparisons of trajectory segments (       ), which is then used to optimize the policy. The reward model optimizes the Bradley-Terry preference probability:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "link": null
    },
